WEBVTT

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.350
There once was a fool living in a certain place.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:20.520
The fool, with good intentions,
taught his older brother how to skate.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.600
His brother was amazingly talented,

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.440
and in no time, he had risen to become
a star in the figure skating world.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:30.230
The fool looked for
a new place in skate-leading.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:27.770
"Young Genius
Reo Shinozaki (11)"

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:29.420
"Reo Shinozaki (13)
Juniors Winner"

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.730
But his brother turned up there, too.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:38.520
The fool made a pact with his brother's
one-time rival, Kensei Maeshima,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.650
and even got the team at Ionodai
involved in his fight against his brother.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:47.690
The fool is me, the brilliant Hayato Sasugai--

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.440
The man who would learn
that everything in his world

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:55.350
would be taken away by
his older brother, Reo Shinozaki.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.650
What a wonderful performance
by St. Clavis Gakuin!

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.480
Now, how about their scores?

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:19.260
Free Skate

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:19.260
Tokyo

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:19.260
St. Clavis Gakuin 
High School

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.980
A technical score of 83.67
and a performance score of 57.17

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.480
for a total of 140.84 for St. Clavis Gakuin!

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.900
This is the highest score
in the history of the series!

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.190
Of course, they've taken the top spot!

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.440
Wow, what an amazing score.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:37.730
Could you say they are pretty much
guaranteed their second consecutive win?

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.190
Yes, well, they really are amazing.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:44.600
Only Ionodai's performance is left now.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.230
It won't be easy for them to beat St. Clavis,

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:50.190
but even so, I want to believe

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.770
in their skating.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:25.470
Episode 12

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:25.470
Sworn Friends

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.310
Now, this year's Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix finals

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.060
is nearing its end.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.560
Will the final school, Ionodai,
come from behind to win,

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:42.440
or will St. Clavis become the first school
to get two consecutive wins?

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.150
It's obvious who'll win.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.350
It's impossible to come from behind now.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.600
Ionodai's going to try for
a solid second place, right?

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.940
They've done enough.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:52.020
They're a public school team that's
only been around for three years?

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.440
They've done well.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.020
They barely have enough club members, right?

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.690
They're outclassed.

00:03:56.690 --> 00:04:00.810
Yeah, it looks like Ionodai
was a little unlucky.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:06.060
Jeez, you guys are unbelievably lucky.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.650
If your short program score
was just a little lower,

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:11.850
then you would probably be trying
for a solid second right now.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:15.190
But you still have a chance to win.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:17.730
Terauchi, you're the pillar of this team.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:20.730
Don't forget to take a broad view
of the team like I taught you.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:21.690
Yes, sir!

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.730
Jonouchi, you tend to go off beat.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.350
Pay attention to the accents in the rhythm.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:26.350
Yessir!

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:29.520
Kiriyama, you're the key to
connecting the team's performance.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:32.230
But this time, focus on your own performance.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.150
You can fulfill your role by doing that.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:34.980
Yes, sir!

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.230
Akimitsu, you tend to look down.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.150
Remind yourself of the
height you need to spot at.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.730
It'll make your performance look lighter.

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:41.600
Yes, sir.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.190
Maeshima, you're the point getter.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:47.940
If you think you can do that thing
we've been working on...

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.190
...then just do it.

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:50.850
Of course.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.440
We'll definitely win.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:53.560
We'll beat them...

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.770
We'll beat that Shinzoaki.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.440
How boring.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.150
I thought you'd be more disheartened,

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.980
and I was looking forward to
figuring out how to get you motivated.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:04.810
My plan's gone to waste.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:07.560
Well, with such a big difference in points...

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:10.810
We just have to do it.
I mean, all we can do is laugh.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:11.900
Yeah!

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:13.900
Well, he's right.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:23.350
Okay, okay. So you're ready to fight back.

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:25.270
Then, let's have a strategy meeting.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:30.400
I feel bad for Ionodai, but we just
got our second win in a row, huh?

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:34.650
It was our personal best! It was amazing.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:36.440
Theory and implementation are different.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.270
All they can do now is...

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:42.400
...act desperate or skate carefully
to become "silver collectors."

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.850
Even so, being the runner-up is praiseworthy.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:01.730
There's not much left for me to say,

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:04.560
and even if I said something,
you'd probably forget it, so just one thing--

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:07.440
If you feel up to it, then just
skate the way you want.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:09.680
Freely, to your heart's content.

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:13.400
Will team skating sixth,
Saitama Prefectural Ionodai High School,

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:10.640
Maeshima.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:13.400
R-Right!

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:14.770
please enter the rink?

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:15.690
Let's go!

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:16.980
Yeah!

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:20.350
The skaters have just come out!

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.350
They are at their starting positions.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:26.940
Last to skate at this year's Boys' High
School Skate-Leading Grand Prix finals

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:27.190
Grand Prix Finals

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.950
Final Performance

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:32.270
is Saitama Prefectural Ionodai High School.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:34.950
Saitama
Inodai High School

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.650
They've started skating.

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:42.940
First is the important start.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:47.400
I hope they keep the aggressive style
everyone loves about them to the end.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:54.520
Did you see that? A triple Axel out of the blue!

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.270
They've abandoned getting second, huh?

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:01.020
They're aiming for a win from behind!

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:04.270
But that's a really steep, thorny path.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:08.230
The pressure of not being able to make
even a single mistake is extraordinary.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:12.270
If just one of them becomes
unable to withstand that pressure,

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:14.060
then it'll all be over.

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:26.730
It's over.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:29.060
Yeah, they can't overtake us now.

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:31.520
Will they switch to aiming for second?

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.480
If they keep up with these attempts,

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.400
then it's possible that we could end up third.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.850
Maeshima's changed it to consecutive jumps.

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:48.230
He's increased the difficulty
of the skills from the initial routine.

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:50.650
Is he trying to cover for the mistakes
by accumulating points for difficulty?

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.440
No, that's not it.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:56.440
Increase the difficulty of the skills?

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.940
But I'm not saying to
push yourselves unreasonably.

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:02.350
Just for the places you think you can do it.

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:05.940
During club, you're always practicing at
a higher level than what you actually skate.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:06.940
Right?

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:07.850
Yeah.

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:09.900
You guys have it, too, right?

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:13.100
Moves you know you can do, that you can jump.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.980
During the performance, put them all out there.

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:18.310
But then the risk of failing...

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.520
Yeah, that's why this is a gamble.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.440
If you mess up, it could all fall apart.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:26.980
The captain and vice-captain's college
recommendations could be revoked, too.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:28.020
What will you do?

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:29.190
Isn't it obvious?

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:32.230
We're not silver collectors aiming for second!

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:35.600
We're challengers trying to push our limits.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.480
Why are they being so reckless?

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.770
Even though there's no chance they could win...

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:51.810
If they mess up, they could end up last. But...

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:52.970
Damn it...

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:53.730
Huh?

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:57.940
This could also be a kind of entertainment.

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:00.940
There are those like my team
who add fun elements,

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:05.690
and those like Shinozaki who perform
perfectly with a high level of skill.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:09.400
This is different. It's the spirit of challenge.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.600
That's right.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.560
What's capturing and moving
the hearts of those watching

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:16.020
is that spirit of never giving up.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.060
Wow...

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.270
They're so cool...

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:25.230
I can't breathe... It hurts...

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:26.730
But...!

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:30.350
If you feel up to it, then just
skate the way you want.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:32.770
You don't need to tell me that!

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:34.060
Again!

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:36.600
Maeshima's pulling those around him again.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:40.850
Once you know how fun this is,
you can't help but try for it again.

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:43.980
Higher... Further...!

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:48.520
What is this? What's going on?

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:54.560
Sho, everyone, we might be able do it now.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.100
Go, Maeshima!

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.350
Not like we could stop you.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.770
Make sure you get those points!

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:01.900
Go!

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.520
Maybe now!

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:15.810
Hey, hey.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:16.730
Don't tell me...

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:18.020
That move...!

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:19.480
It's Mr. Adachi's...

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:20.940
No, it's not!

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:23.520
He's added his own arrangement!

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:47.770
You should be proud, Adachi.

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.480
And Kubota and the others...

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:52.480
Your coaching and management--
the performance just now

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:55.900
was the fruit of all your labor.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:59.400
You should be proud to be a member of this team.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.650
Is it possible? Could it be?

00:11:02.650 --> 00:11:07.020
Yes, that move of Maeshima's especially
could accumulate a lot of points.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.440
I can't believe his captain allowed him
to do something so dangerous.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.230
Terauchi...

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.520
Kiriyama... You okay?

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:19.190
What about you?

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:23.480
Man, I'm beat...

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:26.190
Seriously... But...

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:28.400
I feel great!

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:31.100
Yay... Thanks...

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:34.310
Where's Maeshima?

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:36.690
Maeshima... did a good job...

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:40.350
Yeah, I can't believe he really did it...

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:41.270
Huh?

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:43.100
What are you doing? Hurry up and go back!

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:45.100
They still have to give you your scores.

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:47.310
My body... won't move...

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:48.150
Jeez...

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:49.770
No!

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:51.480
Tomo, go put on your skates.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:52.480
Right!

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:03.100
What, were you so moved that you came over?

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:08.560
There were a lot of people
who said they would beat me.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:11.690
When you ended up being
one of them, it made me sad.

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:13.190
Huh?

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:16.480
Your skating in the past was exciting.

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:18.810
It was so free and composed.

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:21.730
You might not have gotten that many points,

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:25.100
but I learned about expressiveness from you.

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:30.100
Yeah... that's right. Maybe it was admiration...

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:33.060
Maybe I... admired you...

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:36.350
Oh? What's this?

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:40.310
Is that Shinozaki from St. Clavis?

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:44.480
Oh, it looks like he's helping Maeshima.

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:49.150
What you need to surpass
is not me, but yourself.

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:53.980
What you should be after isn't
someone else, but your own ideal.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:55.850
I see it.

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:58.060
That you've surpassed your past self.

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:00.810
You say as you look down on me.

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.350
Well, I'm in a sorry state anyway.
Say what you want.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:09.100
Now, for Ionodai...

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.690
Their scores...

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:13.060
...are here!

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:31.520
It's just us left, huh?

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:33.900
It's kind of lonely, isn't it?

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:35.310
Why did it end up like this...?

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:36.120
Tomo!

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:37.230
Yes?!

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:40.150
Why are you trying to put
everyone in a weird mood?

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:42.100
We haven't graduated yet.

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:44.900
That's not it! They--

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:46.270
Don't tattle!

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:48.770
I mean, you're definitely graduating, right?

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:50.600
So this is a dry run. A dry run!

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:53.690
A dry run for what?

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:56.850
Captain Terauchi, Kiriyama,
sir, congratulations.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.560
I heard you were both accepted
to college through recommendations.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:01.440
Yeah. We'll be skating on the same
team again starting in the spring.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.190
I'll be trying to get in through
the general application.

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:05.310
I mean, we share a common destiny.

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:09.850
We can't let our muscles
go soft before we start college.

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:11.440
We'll keep joining your practices.

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:12.160
Okay!

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.230
Right!

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:14.810
Speaking of which, where's the coach?

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:16.190
I don't know...

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:19.310
He said he had something to do today
and couldn't come to practice, though.

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:23.730
I see. Going back to competing, huh?

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:28.060
Yes. My back has healed, too.
And the unease I felt is gone, too.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:29.900
Because of those boys?

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:32.440
I was only planning on coaching
for a year from the start.

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:35.650
But I won't deny it.

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:39.270
They showed me...

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.230
...that there's no end.

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:44.060
Even the jump sequence I thought was complete

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:47.440
still had possibilities...
still had potential...

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:51.150
Besides, I've been thinking about
something out of character for me.

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:52.900
Out of character?

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:55.190
For the Shinozaki or Himuro generation--

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:57.850
the guys sometimes called
part of the Platinum Age--

00:14:57.850 --> 00:15:00.520
I thought maybe it wouldn't
be too bad to make a path for them.

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:02.400
Really?

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:03.730
Yes.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:06.480
Who will coach that team then?

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:10.020
I heard that they have over
20 people who want to join next year.

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:12.810
That's just about the number they have
on Chutei University High's second string.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:16.900
They already have someone
shrewd who can take my place.

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:21.150
I told them they could
contact me if they need to, too.

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:26.350
The main members this time will probably
also be on the same team in college.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:31.270
However, I didn't tell you all this,
but I will not be your coach in college.

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:33.100
I have decided to stay here.

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:35.480
In order to win next year.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:36.790
What?

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.740
Does that mean there's no interpreter in college?

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:40.020
How will we communicate with those twins?

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:41.600
Hajime, Susumu.

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:47.440
Hajime, I didn't know
you thought so highly of me!

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:49.690
You, too, Susumu?

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:50.340
Kito.

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:51.480
Yes, sir!

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:54.230
With this, you'll be able
to manage in college, too, huh?

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:55.230
Huh?

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.230
For this time's training camp,

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:02.810
we will join teams we competed
against at the Grand Prix finals.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:05.060
We will also have students who plan
to join us from the new school year,

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:07.100
so make sure you don't push them too hard.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:12.020
Let's all work together to learn
what we lack and use it in the future.

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:12.900
That's all.

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:14.270
Yes, sir!

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:18.310
I'm Terahigashi from Hokkaido's Eimei Academy.

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:19.650
I look forward to working with you.

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:22.440
I'm Irie from Ehime's Matsuyama Fukuonji.

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:25.190
There's no need to be serious
all the time, so let's have fun together.

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:26.730
You know what...

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:28.900
I'm the new team captain, Ajikata.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:33.770
Our third years are not here due
to exams, so please bear with us.

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:35.150
I look forward to training with you.

00:16:35.150 --> 00:16:36.770
Thanks.

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:39.060
Um, where's Himekawa?

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:43.310
Sorry, but Izumi had somewhere else to be.

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:46.850
He was asked to join the national team,

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:49.560
so he had to go there suddenly.

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.270
Oh, there you are!

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:52.770
I'm Michinaga.

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:54.690
It's our first time on the same team, right?

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:56.520
If there's anything you
don't understand, let me know.

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:58.350
<i>I'm</i> the captain, though.

00:16:58.350 --> 00:16:59.350
Hello.

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:01.270
You're Himekawa, right?

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:02.980
Your things are here.

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:04.900
Oh, really?

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:06.810
Um... Where is everyone else?

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.600
You're the first one here.

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:12.980
Himekawa, we're aiming
to win the world championship.

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:16.310
In order to get there, practice
will be tough. Prepare yourself.

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:17.690
Bring it on.

