00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:23.940
Speaking of which, Terauchi and Kiriyama

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:25.980
were also both selected
for the national team, right?

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:28.060
You don't need to go today?

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.600
We don't start until next week.

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:31.850
I can't really accept it.

00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:34.560
Why wasn't I chosen?

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:37.400
The selection committee decided it,
so there's nothing you can do about it.

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:38.900
But--

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:42.940
So you guys practice in a public
space for commoners like this?

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:45.440
Number Two Prince? What are you doing here?

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:47.400
I was looking for Maeshima.

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:49.600
I've got good news for him.

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:51.100
Good news? What news?

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:53.190
I found a sponsor.

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:57.060
It's exclusively for overseas, but it looks
like I can keep my promise to him.

00:17:57.060 --> 00:17:58.060
So, where is he?

00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.770
He's out today.

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:01.560
Sasugai is, too.

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:07.230
Ow...!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:09.100
Focus already!

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.440
I am!

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:12.020
Then focus more!

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:14.810
You're the one who said you couldn't
do the move you did in the finals anymore,

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:16.650
so I rented this place for you.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.350
Don't waste it!

00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:20.100
I know.

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:25.440
Shinozaki?

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:26.980
I messed up.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:31.020
I used to skate here a lot, so that
guy knows about this place, too.

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:33.770
Wait, he's still using this place?

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:36.270
So that's how he found out
that I rented it out...

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:39.270
What? What do you want?

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:41.650
Your performance at the finals was wonderful.

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:42.690
And?

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:45.980
It looks like you weren't
chosen for the national team.

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:48.060
I don't care about that.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:49.730
There's still the next Grand Prix Series,

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:51.650
the interscholastic competition,
and the Hyoka Cup.

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:53.900
There's still a ton of stuff left to do.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:58.600
If I was on the national team, too,

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:02.190
I wouldn't be able to keep
all the formations in my head.

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:05.850
Head? I thought you were the type
to remember with your body.

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:07.190
Ever since you were a novice.

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:08.400
Novice...

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:11.440
Oh, yeah, take back what you said back then.

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.650
When you said "You'll never be able to beat me."

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:15.650
I proved that that wasn't true.

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:17.020
From the Grand Prix finals?

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:19.400
From when we were novices! In fifth grade!

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:21.980
Oh.

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:23.600
You forgot?

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:26.980
Back then, I thought...
sooner was better than later...

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:28.230
About what?

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.310
Are you trying to be like the Chutei twins?!

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:32.690
Is Kurayoshi here?

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.560
Someone do something about this guy!

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:37.940
He probably means something like this.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.650
You can understand him, Sasugai?

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:43.900
Back then, you lost your parents
and ended up in a new environment.

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:47.020
Besides, it was just
a little before that, right?

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:50.060
When you started saying that you'd beat him.

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:52.850
So he meant, "if you prioritize winning
and would be happy with a small success,

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:56.850
then with your family situation,
you should just give up now." Right?

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:57.980
Right?

00:19:57.980 --> 00:19:59.100
Yeah.

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:00.690
What the heck?

00:20:00.690 --> 00:20:03.020
If that's what you were trying
to say, then just say it!

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:07.770
Well? What did you come here for, Big Brother?

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:10.020
I've been thinking about it since that day.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:13.560
I could've skated your performance better.

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:16.310
Huh?! Didn't you just say it was wonderful?

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:18.900
It's far from perfect.

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:19.900
Then you should--

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:22.150
At the beginning, you should be like "nyuun."

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:25.770
A "whoo!" there would make
it connect to the next part better!

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:29.060
That's not disciplined enough.
At least a "swoooh..."

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:32.060
After that, there's a "ba-bang!"
so you need to emphasize that!

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:34.100
I understand how you feel,

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:36.350
but you need to listen to your body, too.

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:39.020
I guess I get what you're saying,

00:20:39.020 --> 00:20:40.980
but the part after would be hard with just that.

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:42.230
The footwork, too--

00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:44.310
Like this! 'Cause it looks cool.

00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:45.230
Elegant?

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:46.190
Cool.

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:46.850
Harmonious?

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:49.310
Cool!

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:50.980
Thanks, Sasugai.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:53.730
For working so hard for the team.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:58.060
Especially for bringing Maeshima back.
I have no words to thank you.

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:02.350
Please keep taking care of them--
of Ionodai--from now on, too.

00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:04.520
I want to leave the next stage to you.

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:12.060
I'm grateful for what you said, Captain...

00:21:12.060 --> 00:21:14.350
There you are!

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:16.100
What're you doing in a place like this?

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:18.480
Don't just take a break without saying anything!

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:21.060
I didn't want to get in the way.

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:24.020
So? How was skating with Shinozaki?

00:21:24.020 --> 00:21:25.150
Did you win?

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:27.350
Shut up. Don't ask that.

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:30.650
Oh, yeah. This.

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:31.480
What?

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:33.650
The gold medal from the Grand Prix finals.

00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:35.850
I know. What about it?

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:36.640
You can have it.

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:37.060
Huh?

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:39.150
Half of it, anyway.

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:42.650
Well, I can't split it in two,
so it's still mine, though.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.440
I don't get it.

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:50.230
Because you talked to me that day,
I was able to return to the ice.

00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:54.100
With your strategy and routine,
I was able to get this medal.

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:56.190
I want to do go further with you.

00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:57.900
That's why I'll give you half of it.

00:22:06.060 --> 00:22:07.480
But you can't split it two, right?

00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:09.480
That's why it's the thought that counts.

00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:11.060
Right, right.

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:13.850
We can still fly higher, you know.

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:15.520
Of course.

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:18.690
Further, to a wider world!

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:38.020
I see.

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:41.440
It looks like Maeshima didn't
understand what I was trying to say.

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:44.190
It appears I'm bad at expressing my feelings.

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:46.690
Even if words are supposed
to be used to convey those feelings,

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:49.770
I'm not as good at talking as Hayato.

00:23:49.770 --> 00:23:50.810
Hmm.
